-- npcs: NPC ID = { name, side (omitted: serves both sides), inside (the dungeon they stand in) and
--   insideSpot = { level, x, y } (their spot on its layout map, Data/Maps.lua) }: trainers, book
--   vendors and quest NPCs.
-- quests: quest ID = { name, level (to take it), giver and turnIn (NPC IDs), side (omitted: both),
--   teaches (a recipe's spell ID), skill (the profession skill it needs), inside (its giver's dungeon),
--   needs = { { item ID, count }, ... } }.
-- items: the names of the items the page names, until the game has them.
-- professions: per profession list's ID,
--   ranks: Apprentice to Artisan, each { level, cost (copper), trainers } or, taught by a book,
--   { book, vendors } or, given by a quest, { quests (one per side or one for both), breadcrumbs };
--   specs: { name, spell (known once chosen), skill, level, Alliance and Horde = each side's quest
--   chain as steps of quest IDs (any one of a step's), trainers (shown once the chain is done) };
--   quests: its other quests, by level, a quest ID or a group shown as one line { label = what
--   they are for, quest ID, ... }; nodes (Mining, Herbalism): what it gathers, lowest skill first,
--   each { item ID, the skill it needs (orange), yellow from, green from, grey from, rich (the rich
--   vein of an ore another vein gives too) }; farm: per skill band { low, high, zones = { { map
--   (uiMapID), spots (where the band's nodes or beasts spawn), side (the side it is safe for;
--   omitted: contested), nodes (the nodes found there that give skill-ups in the band, by their
--   place in nodes) or levels (Skinning: the band's beast levels found there) }, ... } }.
